techaviv-betterhelp:greenhouse:422177100.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;UpLift &amp;amp; BetterHelp – Redefining Access to Mental Healthcare&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At UpLift, we believe mental health is just as important as physical health — and we&#39;re rethinking the mental healthcare model. UpLift is a multi-sided marketplace, applying technology to empower patients to find Therapists and Psychiatric providers covered by their insurance plan.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While 1 in 5 Americans struggle with mental health issues, only 40% of this group received care in the last year. At the same time, only 30% of therapists accept insurance. UpLift acts as the bridge between patient, provider, and insurer — empowering patients to find the best care for their needs at a price they can afford.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join UpLift&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible earnings model*:&lt;/strong&gt; Compensation includes both patient care and collaboration activities. Physicians can earn $25 per assigned supervision slot (in capped states) and $30 per completed chart review. Total monthly earnings may vary based on state coverage and activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expand access to care:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide psychiatric services to individuals who otherwise may not have access to mental healthcare.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative model:&lt;/strong&gt; Support and supervise Nurse Practitioners (NPs) through formal collaboration agreements, including chart reviews and consultation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All-in-one virtual platform:&lt;/strong&gt; Focus on your patients — UpLift handles credentialing, enrollment, and platform operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work from anywhere:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is 100% remote, with care delivered via UpLift’s purpose-built telemedicine platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible commitment:&lt;/strong&gt; Part-time, 1099 contract position with autonomy over your clinical schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct video consultations and communicate with patients via telemedicine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess, diagnose, and treat patients, including prescribing medication when clinically appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide supervision and oversight to Nurse Practitioners (NPs) in states requiring collaborative agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete required chart reviews and provide timely consultation support to NPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain responsiveness for collaboration duties in accordance with state requirements and UpLift standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate care with UpLift’s network of therapists and other providers to ensure high-quality outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide empathetic, evidence-based care while upholding UpLift’s clinical and service standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share product and workflow feedback with UpLift’s engineering and operations teams to help improve care delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Board-certified Psychiatrist with active clinical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active and unrestricted medical license(s) in one or more of the following priority states: Virginia, Texas, Florida, Georgia, or North Carolina.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-state licensure strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supervising or collaborating with Psychiatric Nurse Practitioners (e.g. NPs) is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable prescribing medication when clinically appropriate and permitted by state law.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at using online tools and technology to deliver virtual care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to provide timely consultation support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous telemedicine experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important to Know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a part-time, contract (1099) position — not a salaried employee role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physicians may set their own schedules for patient care; however, collaboration responsibilities require ongoing responsiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physicians may stop seeing patients at any time, but collaborative agreement responsibilities require a 120-day wind-down period to ensure continuity of care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation structure varies by state depending on collaboration requirements (capped vs. uncapped states).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UpLift will credential and enroll you with multiple health plans to expand access to insured patients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All care is delivered remotely through UpLift’s telehealth platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All clinical decisions are made independently by licensed providers in accordance with state telehealth laws and professional standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;License/Certification:&lt;/strong&gt; Medical License (Required)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Georgia&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Compensation is paid on a per-activity basis and is not a guaranteed hourly wage or salary amount. Actual earnings vary based on state-requirements, completed activities, patient care activity, and other operational factors.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

